# Component Architecture / コンポーネント・アーキテクチャ

## Layer Model / レイヤーモデル

```
UI (React Components)
  ↓ calls only
Application Services (use cases, server actions, API routes)
  ↓ orchestrates
Domain (entities, value objects, domain services)
  ↓ persisted via
Repositories / Providers (interfaces + implementations)
```

## Hard Rules / 厳守事項

1. **UI must NOT call Repository or Provider directly.** Components, hooks, and pages consume Application Services or typed API clients that wrap services.
2. **Providers are swappable implementations** behind interfaces (research, LLM, storage). UI never imports `SearXNGProvider` or similar.
3. **Never expose secrets to the client** — API keys, service role keys, and provider tokens stay server-side only.

## Type Safety / 型安全

- Strict TypeScript everywhere; `strict: true` in tsconfig.
- Avoid `any`; use `unknown` + narrowing, Zod schemas at boundaries, and explicit DTO types for UI props.
- Domain types live in shared packages; UI receives **view models**, not raw DB rows.

## Component Guidelines / コンポーネント指針

- **Presentational vs container**: presentational components receive data + callbacks; data fetching in server components or service hooks.
- One primary action per action bar; secondary actions as subdued buttons or menu items.
- Don't wrap every row in a Card — use `TableRow`, `ListItem`, or semantic `<li>`.
- No large rounded card grids; radius 6–12px on structural elements.

## Product Alignment / プロダクト整合

- Components map to **work units** (案件カード、タスクリスト、成果物エディタ), not to backend module names.
- This is a **business OS** — components support workflows, not chat bubbles as the default primitive.
- Mobile components are purpose-designed (bottom sheets, compact rows), not stacked desktop columns.

## Completion Gates / 完了条件

```bash
npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm run test && npm run build
```

All must pass before merging UI or service-layer changes.
